---
<section class="italics">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Italics</p>
      <h2>A true italic, not a slanted afterthought.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        The italic has its own rhythm: a single-storey <i>a</i> and <i>g</i>,
        flowing <i>k l j r v w t f</i> drawn in the spirit of Recursive Mono
        Linear, and a straight, quiet <i>x</i>. It's perfect for comments,
        keywords and emphasis without turning your code into calligraphy.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="compare card">
      <div class="row">
        <span class="label">Upright</span>
        <span class="glyphs">afgjklrtvwx</span>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <span class="label">Italic</span>
        <span class="glyphs" style="font-style:italic">afgjklrtvwx</span>
      </div>
      <pre class="snippet"><code><span class="c">// fetch the user, then render the view</span>
<span class="k">let</span> view = <span class="k">await</span> <span class="f">load</span>(user);</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr; gap: 56px; align-items: center; }
  .compare { padding: 28px; }
  .row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 90px 1fr; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .label { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
  .glyphs { font-size: clamp(36px, 5.2vw, 64px); line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: .02em; }
  .snippet { margin: 22px 0 0; font: inherit; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; white-space: pre-wrap; }
  .snippet .c { color: var(--tok-com); font-style: italic; }
  .snippet .k { color: var(--tok-kw); font-style: italic; }
  .snippet .f { color: var(--tok-fn); }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; } }
</style>
